WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.439 --> 00:00:08.560
Released to celebrate the 20th anniversary
of Nintendo's original Pokemon game, Pokemon

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:11.620
Go has become an instant sensation.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:16.810
More than 15 million people downloaded the
free game in its first week, with more active

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:20.580
daily users than Twitter, Facebook, and Snapchat.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:25.680
Let's look behind what's already one of the
most popular smartphone games around.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.790
Google Earth Origins

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:32.340
Pokemon Go combines online gaming with GPS-linked
map technology.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.289
And both of those technologies were pioneered
by the same man.

00:00:36.289 --> 00:00:43.670
Back in 1996, 21-year-old John Hanke created
Meridian 59, the first "massively multiplayer

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:49.050
online game," where gamers could connect globally
over the Internet to explore the game's world

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:51.129
and compete against one another.

00:00:51.129 --> 00:00:57.420
In 2000, Hanke developed Keyhole, a system
linking roads and highways with aerial photography

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:02.350
to create the first-ever GPS-linked, 3D map
of the world.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:06.820
Hanke later sold Keyhole to Google, where
it became Google Earth.

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:11.360
Hanke went on to spearhead Google Maps and
Google Street View.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:12.940
Inspired By A Joke

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:17.440
Each April Fools Day, Google pulls light-hearted
pranks on its users.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.280
In 2014, they announced the Google Maps Pokemon
Challenge.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:28.500
"We've prepared the most rigorous test known
to man to find the world's best Pokemon Master."

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:33.600
Teaming up with The Pokemon Company and Nintendo,
the program was a fake game that supposedly

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:38.310
allowed users to capture Pokemon creatures
hidden in the real world, that they could

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:40.270
find with Google Maps.

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:45.530
So many people desperately wanted it to be
real that the prank went viral, and just two

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:50.520
years later, that basic concept became Pokemon
Go.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:51.830
Ingress 2

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:57.690
With funding from Google, Hanke launched Niantic
Labs in 2010 to add a gaming layer to Maps.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:03.390
There, he created a game called Ingress, the
first MMO that involved the use of gamers'

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:04.800
real-world locations.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:08.450
It was basically Pokemon Go except without
the Pokemon.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:13.780
The most popular user-generated meeting points
in Ingress later became the Pokestops and

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:15.970
Gyms in Pokemon Go.

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:17.080
Poke-Fakes

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:22.420
Pokemon Go became available for Android and
iPhone users in North America, Australia,

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.910
and New Zealand on July 6, 2016.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:28.740
It hit Europe and most of Asia on July 15.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:34.160
That nine-day gap was too much for some, who
downloaded the bootleg or knockoff versions

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:35.450
of Pokemon Go.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:40.950
In fact, at least 43 separate fake versions
of Pokemon Go have been spotted, many of which

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:45.360
are malicious apps that flood users' phones
with ads and malware.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:50.630
Worse, some of these bootlegs could take control
of the user's phone without their knowledge,

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:52.470
mining their personal data.

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:55.610
The hunter has become 
the hunted.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:02:59.920
(yells)

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:02.360
"Retreat!"

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:03.720
Banned In Saudi Arabia

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:10.140
Pokemon Go is gaining popularity in the Middle
East, and clerics in Saudi Arabia are skeptical,

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.290
to say the least.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:16.860
They've issued a fatwa, or "Islamic religious
ban" on the game, which follows up a previous

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:20.610
fatwa against the original Pokemon games from
1996.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:25.750
According to them, the game's trading-card
aspect "encouraged blasphemy and gambling."

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:31.819
While Pokemon Go might not use cards, it does
apparently contain "forbidden images," like

00:03:31.819 --> 00:03:35.380
symbols that could be mistaken for Masonic
symbolism.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:38.140
In other words, Jigglypuff is the devil.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:44.200
(Jiggly Puff singing)

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:46.740
Get Up And Move!

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:47.940
Or Don't.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:52.900
While the game helps people get more exercise
as they walk around searching for Pokemon,

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:56.120
some still prefer their video games to be
less dangerous.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:01.610
"Actually two people in San Diego fell off
a cliff while playing the game."

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:06.910
Crafty entrepreneurs in cities like New York,
San Francisco, and Portland have placed ads

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:11.910
on Craigslist, offering to drive players around
while they Poke-hunt.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:16.690
Some drivers even promise to provide the one
thing coveted by players even more than a

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:21.049
Legendary Mew: phone chargers.

00:04:21.049 --> 00:04:22.280
Thanks for watching!

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:25.970
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:29.520
And leave us a comment to let us know which
Pokemon you've caught today…

